34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems my suspicions were well-founded. Some elements of our previous schemes have aged like fine wine, while others have vanished like a summer mist.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"I've found that we have very few firms willing to do the heavy lifting here. They are cautious about the soil, which suggests a high risk of delays.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh boy, the numbers are scary! The cost to keep the green parts is way higher than the paved parts, and it's only getting more expensive!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The staffing situation is critical. The permanent roll has shrunk significantly. We are relying far too much on bought-in services and a dwindling number of staff.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data confirms my fears. The site is overheating and the drainage is failing. Furthermore, people are ignoring the paths and cutting across the grass to reach the tram.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, that is fascinating. If the public is already carving their own paths, any plan that ignores these ""desire lines"" will simply be destroyed by the users.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Asuka, if the staffing is low and the contractors are few, we cannot afford a plan with a complex construction phase or high-maintenance features.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! If we pick a plan with tons of fancy gardens, we're just signing a check for a disaster in three years! We need something simple!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,I agree. We cannot propose a plan that requires a full-time presence if the city is cutting the rota. We need a low-intervention design.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"We must prioritize a plan that addresses the drainage issues and respects the actual flow of pedestrians, rather than forcing them into artificial paths.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are in agreement. We need a plan that is robust, low-maintenance, and respects the natural behavior of the citizens.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"I am particularly worried about the ""diggers"" phase. If the soil is as tricky as the firms suggest, a plan with massive excavation will likely drift past the deadline.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm just thinking about the money! @Misaki, does that mean we should avoid the plans with the big new ponds or underground structures?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"Yes. Ponds require constant cleaning and specialized staff. If the roll is down to seven people, we can't manage that.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,A plan that fights the ground will lose. We need a design that works with the existing drainage failures and the heat island effect.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall be looking for the candidate that prioritizes durability over aesthetics. A simple, well-built path is better than a gold-plated one that cracks in two years.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I will vote for the plan that minimizes heavy earth-moving and has a realistic phasing strategy.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for the one that's cheapest to keep! No fancy stuff that costs a fortune every year!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I will support the plan that requires the least amount of daily human intervention. We cannot staff a luxury park.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,I will vote for the plan that acknowledges the tram-stop traffic and provides sustainable drainage solutions.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
