60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Plan A is the most honest. Paving is durable, and it doesn't rely on the hope that someone remembers to water the trees for five years.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Plan A also requires the least amount of deep excavation compared to the ponds in C or the facilities in D. It is the safest bet for the timeline.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,Plan A is perfect! Paving is way cheaper to maintain than gardens or ponds! No more scary upkeep bills for the city!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Plan A is the only logical choice. It requires minimal daily groundskeeping and doesn't need a specialized staff to keep it from falling apart.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Plan A is the only one that solves the problems. Paving the main crossing routes to the tram stop stops the grass from being destroyed, and the shade structures address the heat.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is rare to see such immediate consensus. It seems we have all found the same flaw in the more ""ambitious"" designs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,The risk of soil slippage and contractor shortages makes Plan C and D far too dangerous for the city's budget and schedule.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,Yay! I'm so glad we all agree! Let's go with the one that won't make the finance people cry in three years!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,It is the only plan that respects the reality of the current staffing rota. We cannot maintain a woodland or a wetland with seven people.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"It is the only plan that doesn't fight the people. By paving the areas they already use, we work with the behavior of the city.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I must admit, I find it slightly amusing that the ""boring"" option is the only one that is actually intelligent.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"In this case, boring is reliable. I can sleep soundly knowing the project won't be half-finished when the next election comes around.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,Boring is great if it means we don't run out of money! I'm totally on board with the Market Plaza!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Logic dictates that we choose the option with the lowest failure rate. Plan A is the only one that fits our constraints.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I am satisfied. It is a pragmatic choice that addresses the drainage, the heat, and the pedestrian flow without overextending our resources.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Then we are decided. Let us proceed to the vote.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,Ready!,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
